   174	## 3. Exact Alexander polynomial of the primitive packet
   175	
   176	The preceding report froze the positive bands
   177	
   178	```text
   179	b1 = s1,
   180	b2 = s2^3 s1 s2^(-3),
   181	b3 = s3 s2^3 s1 s2^(-3) s3^(-1),
   182	n  = s2 s3^2 s2^(-1),                                  (3.1)
   183	```
   184	
   185	and their product
   186	
   187	```text
   188	beta = b1 b2 b3 n
   189	 = s1 s2^3 s1 s2^(-3)
   190	      s3 s2^3 s1 s2^(-3) s3^(-1)
   191	      s2 s3^2 s2^(-1).                                 (3.2)
   192	```
   193	
   194	The permutation of (3.2) is a four-cycle, so its closure is a knot.  Recall
   195	that the three simple bands in (3.1) have tree incidence and Euler number
   196	one, while `n` supplies the one positive two-point `(2,2)` identification.
   197	The based color tuple from the charged report is fixed by every factor and
   198	generates `S4`.
   199	
   200	For transparency, use the unreduced Burau generator whose nontrivial block is
   201	
   202	```text
   203	rho(s_i) = [[1-t, t],
   204	            [1,   0]],                                  (3.3)
   205	```
   206	
   207	and let `bar(rho)` be its quotient by the invariant vector.  For a four-braid
   208	whose closure is a knot,
   209	
   210	```text
   211	Delta_closed(beta)(t)
   212	  = (1-t)/(1-t^4) det(I-bar(rho)(beta))                 (3.4)
   213	```
   214	
   215	up to `+/-t^j`.  Exact Laurent arithmetic applied to (3.2) yields (0.2).  In
   216	dense high-to-low Laurent coefficients this is
   217	
   218	```text
   219	-t^6 + 6t^5 - 15t^4 + 25t^3 - 31t^2 + 33t - 31
   220	      + 25t^(-1) - 15t^(-2) + 6t^(-3) - t^(-4).        (3.5)
   221	```
   222	
   223	It is normalized by `Delta_beta(1)=1`.  Put
   224	
   225	```text
   226	P(t)=t^6-4t^5+4t^4-3t^3+4t^2-4t+1.                   (3.6)
   227	```
   228	
   229	Then
   230	
   231	```text
   232	P(2)=-15,                 P(3)=25.                     (3.7)
   233	```
