   235	The intermediate value theorem gives a real zero `r` with `2<r<3`.  In
   236	particular `|r|` is not one, so `r` is not a root of unity.  Equations
   237	(2.3) and (3.7) contradict the existence of a one-place polynomial curve
   238	whose complete boundary braid is (3.2).
