   268	## 5. Exact global one-node control
   269	
   270	The obstruction is checked against the polynomial parametrization (0.5).
   271	If `(X(t),Y(t))=(X(u),Y(u))`, then `t^2=u^2`.  For `t != u` this forces
   272	`u=-t`, and
   273	
   274	```text
   275	X(t)-X(-t)=2t(t^2-1).                                  (5.1)
   276	```
   277	
   278	The only nontrivial unordered identified pair is therefore `{+1,-1}`.  The
   279	derivative is
   280	
   281	```text
   282	(X'(t),Y'(t))=(4t^3+3t^2-1,2t).                        (5.2)
   283	```
   284	
   285	When `Y'` vanishes, `t=0` and `X'=-1`; thus the normalization map is an
   286	immersion.  At the two points above the unique double point `(1,1)`, the
   287	tangent vectors are
