   293	
   294	The double point is ordinary.  Eliminating `t` gives the irreducible image
   295	equation
   296	
   297	```text
   298	(x-y^2)^2-y(y-1)^2=0.                                  (5.4)
   299	```
   300	
   301	There are no other affine singularities: away from the unique identified
   302	pair the normalization is injective and immersive.  Since both coordinate
   303	functions have their sole pole at `t=infinity`, the curve has one
   304	normalization place at infinity.
   305	
   306	Project (5.4) to the `y`-line.  At `y=0`, `t=0` gives one simple ramification
   307	and the positive braid factor `s1`.  At `y=1`, the ordinary node gives
   308	`s1^2`.  Thus
   309	
   310	```text
   311	beta_infinity_control=s1^3,                             (5.5)
   312	```
   313	
   314	whose closure is the trefoil.  Zariski--van Kampen on fibre meridians `a,b`
   315	gives
   316	
   317	```text
   318	pi1(A2-B_control)
   319	 = <a,b | a=b, [a,b]=1>
   320	 = Z.                                                   (5.6)
   321	```
